{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0171BKTnU55DTgZCtQHuYaNn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"ClimateNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://nlp4climate.github.io/submissionguide/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - acl-org/emnlp-2026: Repository for the EMNLP 2026 conference · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/emnlp-2026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some information about EMNLP 2026 reviewer processes and timelines, though specific details about the complete reviewer guidelines review form were not fully detailed in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n## Review Timeline\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Review Process Overview\nSubmissions and reviews will be performed via the Open Review platform, where authors submit articles to ARR to receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors, then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026, where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions from the ARR reviews and meta-reviews.\n\n## Reviewer Registration\nAll authors must complete the author registration form by May 27, 2026 EoD AoE.\n\nThe search results indicate that the detailed reviewer guidelines and review form exist, but the specific content of the EMNLP 2026 review form itself wasn't provided in these results. The results did include information about the EMNLP 2020 review form structure, but EMNLP 2026 may have different guidelines. For the most current and complete reviewer guidelines for EMNLP 2026, I'd recommend checking the official EMNLP 2026 website at 2026.emnlp.org or the Open Review platform where reviews are submitted.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92ec98e3-e572-42db-9ebd-25eabdb3cb35","uuid":"a7cddd60-3337-4a59-ba77-43aa47b005f9","timestamp":"2026-05-13T10:12:02.442Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011ayQ9XaiZ1NfbUqCve73co","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"ClimateNLP 2026","url":"https://nlp4climate.github.io/submissionguide/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"GitHub - acl-org/emnlp-2026: Repository for the EMNLP 2026 conference · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/emnlp-2026"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some information about EMNLP 2026 reviewer processes and timelines, though specific details about the complete reviewer guidelines review form were not fully detailed in these results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n## Review Timeline\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Review Process Overview\nSubmissions and reviews will be performed via the Open Review platform, where authors submit articles to ARR to receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors, then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026, where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions from the ARR reviews and meta-reviews.\n\n## Reviewer Registration\nAll authors must complete the author registration form by May 27, 2026 EoD AoE.\n\nThe search results indicate that the detailed reviewer guidelines and review form exist, but the specific content of the EMNLP 2026 review form itself wasn't provided in these results. The results did include information about the EMNLP 2020 review form structure, but EMNLP 2026 may have different guidelines. For the most current and complete reviewer guidelines for EMNLP 2026, I'd recommend checking the official EMNLP 2026 website at 2026.emnlp.org or the Open Review platform where reviews are submitted."],"durationSeconds":6.3452850629999995}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018671daT6qgJfqLttCwL5x4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring practices. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2025 Reviewer Guidelines and Scoring\n\nThe review form was adapted from ACL 2020 and EMNLP 2020 and consists of four main sections.\n\n### Scoring Scale\nA 5-point scale with half-point increments is used. A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, and reviewers are encouraged to take a stand on whether the paper is above or below the borderline by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, though if a paper is truly borderline, a rating of 3 should be used.\n\n### Review Form Structure\nThe In-Depth Review section includes a core review subsection, which is the most important part and should include the reviewer's view of the main contributions the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds, as well as significant strong and weak parts of the paper and the work it describes.\n\n### Reproducibility Assessment\nThe review form asks \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility? Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" with scores of 1-5, with detailed explanations for each point level provided in the review form.\n\nThe official EMNLP 2025 reviewer instructions page is available at https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/ for more detailed information.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92ec98e3-e572-42db-9ebd-25eabdb3cb35","uuid":"6d6c7108-5401-42a4-ab6c-6de33201511e","timestamp":"2026-05-13T10:12:03.466Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Vf3jZtk7bh1T8fATrPy1Sa","content":[{"title":"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ"},{"title":"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring practices. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2025 Reviewer Guidelines and Scoring\n\nThe review form was adapted from ACL 2020 and EMNLP 2020 and consists of four main sections.\n\n### Scoring Scale\nA 5-point scale with half-point increments is used. A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, and reviewers are encouraged to take a stand on whether the paper is above or below the borderline by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, though if a paper is truly borderline, a rating of 3 should be used.\n\n### Review Form Structure\nThe In-Depth Review section includes a core review subsection, which is the most important part and should include the reviewer's view of the main contributions the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds, as well as significant strong and weak parts of the paper and the work it describes.\n\n### Reproducibility Assessment\nThe review form asks \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility? Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" with scores of 1-5, with detailed explanations for each point level provided in the review form.\n\nThe official EMNLP 2025 reviewer instructions page is available at https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/ for more detailed information."],"durationSeconds":6.894819124000001}}
