c details about a 1-5 overall assessment scoring scale for the review form. \n\nThe search results show the review form page and reviewer guidelines, but they don't display the specific scoring scale definitions. For more detailed information about the exact scoring scale values (1-5) and how each level is defined, you would need to access the full review form directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or consult the detailed reviewer guidelines.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92ec98e3-e572-42db-9ebd-25eabdb3cb35","uuid":"e1570cd0-4fb7-4897-96d0-9202ae86941e","timestamp":"2026-05-13T10:12:12.285Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment scoring scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01MsdPxedNitKHfEtic1YG2r","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"ACL ARR | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 October | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FOctober"}]},"I found information about the ACL Rolling Review scoring system. Starting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. However, the search results don't contain specific details about a 1-5 overall assessment scoring scale for the review form. \n\nThe search results show the review form page and reviewer guidelines, but they don't display the specific scoring scale definitions. For more detailed information about the exact scoring scale values (1-5) and how each level is defined, you would need to access the full review form directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform or consult the detailed reviewer guidelines."],"durationSeconds":4.058227327000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y8o1J74WS2TbdgnkfSam3C","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment soundness novelty\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Response to ACL 2023 Questions\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Changelog\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Arr Changes December\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ARR-changes-December/\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"}]\n\nI found the search results from the ACL Rolling Review website. Here are the relevant findings about the review form's assessment criteria:\n\n## Overall Assessment and Soundness\n\nThe review form asks whether a paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, and whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them. For experimental papers, reviewers consider the depth and/or breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation. For position papers and surveys, they consider whether the current state of the field is adequately represented and main counter-arguments acknowledged. For resource papers, they consider data collection methodology, resulting data, and differences from existing resources.\n\n## Confidence and Novelty\n\nA confidence level of 2 indicates the reviewer is willing to defend their evaluation, but it is fairly likely they missed some details, didn't understand some central points, or can't be sure about the novelty of the work.\n\n## Scoring System Update\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The overall assessment is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92ec98e3-e572-42db-9ebd-25eabdb3cb35","uuid":"a25191b2-4ce2-4269-a9aa-9801f65ded9a","timestamp":"2026-05-13T10:12:14.547Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment soundness novelty","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Qk4PqVLSGkmvwiSQWQqHLD","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Response to ACL 2023 Questions","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"ARR Changelog","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/changelog"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"Arr Changes December","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ARR-changes-December/"},{"title":"Incentives 2026","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"}]},"I found the search results from the ACL Rolling Review website. Here are the relevant findings about the review form's assessment criteria:\n\n## Overall Assessment and Soundness\n\nThe review form asks whether a paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, and whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them. For experimental papers, reviewers consider the depth and/or breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation. For position papers and surveys, they consider whether the current state of the field is adequately represented and main counter-arguments acknowledged. For resource papers, they consider data collection methodology, resulting data, and differences from existing resources.\n\n## Confidence and Novelty\n\nA confidence level of 2 indicates the reviewer is willing to defend their evaluation, but it is fairly likely they missed some details, didn't understand some central points, or can't be sure about the novelty of the work.\n\n## Scoring System Update\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The overall assessment is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and other factors like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":5.850783501000001}}
