{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ybm8a2hiYAyzua3vTQZ9Qq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL rolling review \"overall assessment\" \"1\" \"2\" \"3\" \"4\" \"5\" scoring scale definition review form 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 July | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FJuly\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 October | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FOctober\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for the detailed scoring scale definitions:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"Response to ACL 2023 Questions\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Allen Cognitive Level - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK556125/\"},{\"title\":\"Anterior Cruciate Ligament OsteoArthritis Score (ACLOAS): Longitudinal MRI-based whole joint assessment of anterior cruciate ligament injury - PubMed\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24657830/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2022 Chair Blog Post FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://www.2022.aclweb.org/post/acl-2022-chair-blog-post-faq\"}]\n\nLet me search for the specific overall assessment scale definitions:\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"Survivors, Complainers, and Borderliners: Upward Bias in Online Discussions of Academic Conference Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.16831v1\"},{\"title\":\"Intructions for Reviewers - ACL 2020\",\"url\":\"https://acl2020.org/reviewers/\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for the complete overall assessment scale with all five definitions:\n\nNo links found.\n\nBased on the search results I've gathered, I can provide you with information about the ACL Rolling Review overall assessment scoring scale for 2025:\n\n## ACL ARR 2025 Overall Assessment Scoring Scale\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nFrom the review form, here are the definitions found for the overall assessment scale:\n\n**Soundness scoring (1-5):**\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims. Some minor points may need extra support or details.\n- 2 = Poor: Some of the main claims are not sufficiently supported. There are major technical/methodological problems.\n- 1 = Major Issues: This study is not yet sufficiently thorough to warrant publication or is not relevant to ACL.\n\n**Excitement scoring (1-5):**\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 3 = Interesting: I might mention some points of this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference if there's time.\n- 2 = Potentially Interesting: this paper does not resonate with me, but it might with others in the *ACL community.\n- 1 = Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community\n\nThe search results did not provide the complete detailed definitions for all five levels of the overall assessment score itself. You may find the complete overall assessment scale by visiting the ARR review form directly at http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92ec98e3-e572-42db-9ebd-25eabdb3cb35","uuid":"abaf072d-cd9c-4920-a497-3499b5207e84","timestamp":"2026-05-13T10:12:33.146Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL rolling review \"overall assessment\" \"1\" \"2\" \"3\" \"4\" \"5\" scoring scale definition review form 2025","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EXgezDtrGqN6iJicYGRDqn","content":[{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 July | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FJuly"},{"title":"ACL ARR